Solve the following problem in C++:

# PROBLEM DESCRIPTION START

You are given a map represented by a grid of size 32xN. Each cell in the grid is either land (represented by '1') or water (represented by '0'). The map is encoded as a vector of N integers, where each integer represents a row in the grid; y=0 is the first value and y=N-1 is the last row. Within each integer, the Most Significant Bit (MSB) represents x=0 and the Least Significant Bit (LSB) represents x=31.

You are tasked with finding the size of the largest contiguous landmass on the map. A landmass is defined as a group of connected land cells, where connectedness is defined in 4 directions (up, down, left, right).
# PROBLEM DESCRIPTION END

